# Provenance: licensing-capability-matrix.yml run 34989114739 (2026-09-15),
# 2020.3.49f1 / personal, the `return-license` half. Trimmed to the licensing
# lines; access tokens are masked as Unity masks them.
#
# A return that plainly succeeded, containing two lines a naive grader reads as
# failure:
#
#   - "An error occured while trying to return the ULF license. Ulf license
#     file not found" - the ULF route does not apply to a Personal seat, and
#     the script says so and switches routes. It is the beginning of the
#     success, not a failure.
#   - "[Licensing::Module] Error: Serial number unavailable for ULF return" -
#     printed on the same successful path, after the entitlement has already
#     been handed back.
#
# Grading on the presence of "Error" or on the absence of a known failure
# string gets this cell wrong in both directions, which is the whole argument
# for lv_return_verdict's ordering: success evidence first, everything else
# afterwards.
[Licensing::Module] Successfully connected to LicensingClient on channel: "LicenseClient-root"
